WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.733
(soft classical instrumental music)

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.080
- So its 11 o'clock.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.630
We are now almost driving around one hour

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.723
for Puffin patrol security thing.

00:00:22.761 --> 00:00:26.380
There's one, there's one, there's one.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.213
Be careful.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.073
Yes, we got one.

00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:30.686
Elfie, hand me the net.

00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:33.686
(loud horn honking)

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.543
Come here.

00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:39.863
(loud horn honking)

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.870
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.463
Got it.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.320
- My goodness.
- My goodness.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.400
You are drama queen.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.783
You are drama queen.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.823
Yes, everything is fine.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.616
Now you're happy.

00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:04.673
- [Elfie] Sweetheart, yes.

00:01:08.324 --> 00:01:11.824
(soft instrumental music)

00:01:17.252 --> 00:01:18.380
- Newfoundland, the place and the land

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.830
and the ocean is just as
much a character in our lives

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.850
as your brother or sister.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.240
You know, we've always been that way

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.853
because we're isolated; we're an island.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.890
Everything here is so interconnected

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:36.080
and people feel that because they have to.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.180
It was the only way they could survive.

00:01:43.248 --> 00:01:46.331
(loud motor revving)

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.600
- Less than two kilometers
from the coastlines

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.250
of Witless Bay is the Witless
Bay Ecological Reserve.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.190
It's a group of islands that's spread out

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.660
from the Witless Bay region,

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.480
and they're home to the Atlantic Puffin,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.203
Newfoundland's iconic bird.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.243
There's over 600,000 pairs
of Puffins on these islands.

00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:15.960
They mate every year.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.230
They go to sea for four years,

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.530
and when they come back
they keep coming here.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.090
There's records showing
that we have Puffins

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.960
that are up to 20 and 30 years old there,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.410
and they come to the same burrows.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.470
So it's really important

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.590
that this ecological
reserve was established

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:31.793
to protect these birds.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.730
If you look around the community now,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.590
they advertise it's the
home of the Atlantic Puffin

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.860
and some of their facilities
are named after a Puffin,

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.338
the school mascot is a Puffin.

00:02:44.338 --> 00:02:46.880
So it's something that
people are proud of.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.530
Everybody can resonate with them.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.790
- The Puffin generates a
lot of revenue in tourism

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.220
in Newfoundland and
especially in this local area

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.643
and it creates a lot of jobs.

00:03:00.574 --> 00:03:02.583
- It's a big icon for
tourism in Newfoundland.

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.170
A Puffin, it's our provincial bird.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:08.163
So we've really got to look after them.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.090
- It has sort of always been a thing.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.930
We would see the birds
squat all over the road

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.090
and different things and
we just knew, obviously,

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.420
they were confused.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.080
But we didn't know anything about that

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.830
until into the 2000s.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.480
That's when we started to
learn what the problem was.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:35.690
It could of been many people
who came into our town

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.310
and started the Puffin patrol.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.790
And there would of been resistance

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.320
because it would of been
the whole "your an outsider,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.020
"how are you telling us what to do?"

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.347
But this is unique because it was Juergen.

00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:48.220
- And you want to look
me in the camera right?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.390
- Me.
- No, you can look...

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.070
- Oh, to you, okay good, okay that's good.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:56.940
- His presence is vast,
and it's very open.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.740
Everybody knows Juergen.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.750
- It's beautiful, yeah.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.630
When I go to the post office or the shop,

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.643
they say, hey Puffin man, and
I think it's a compliment.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.190
I wouldn't call me a real environmentalist

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.040
because I know people
who do this do much more

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.870
than what I'm doing.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.923
But we just taking care as I learned it.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.380
I think it's normal to
do things like this.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.023
When you see something, it's
wrong, try to change it.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.870
- I met Juergen a long time ago.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.653
He was in filmmaking and he had quite

00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:40.513
an array of movie stars.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.450
He's his own character.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.080
He beats his own drum.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.560
- And I love this air.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.823
It's like champagne

00:04:48.823 --> 00:04:51.420
It's so wonderful here.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.520
- I'm so grateful, and
we're all so grateful

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.710
that he came in, he saw the situation

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.010
and people just then
stirred the common gator

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.730
and just feel good about doing something

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.710
for their community.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.680
- I want to know tonight,
it's Puffin patrol again.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.360
Are you ready?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.330
It was in August and our family,

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.350
we watched on the road dead little birds.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.630
- [Reporter] During the day Juergen

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.630
often finds other Puffins
on the Witless Bay roads

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.870
who are not so lucky.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.350
- Every year hundreds of young Puffins,

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.543
those birds with colorful beaks,

00:05:20.543 --> 00:05:23.190
lose their way in the
waters off Newfoundland

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.060
and Labrador ending up
on a wing in a prayer.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.295
- [Man] The little Puffins
have been getting lost in town.

00:05:28.295 --> 00:05:31.800
- So I was asking people
here around, what is it?

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:32.940
And they told me don't touch it,

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.400
their poison has been always there.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.910
But I thought, something is wrong.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.030
What could it be?

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:41.060
And then you find out that this
little dead bird on the road

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.090
are little Puffin chicks.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.748
You learn that they come out in the night

00:05:44.748 --> 00:05:47.470
and they look for light,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.230
moonlight in their instinct.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.925
But they have no idea, is
it moonlight, traffic light,

00:05:51.925 --> 00:05:54.753
a car light or garage
light, whatever it is,

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:57.290
they say light is light, let's go for it.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.280
So they fly, then they stand
in the middle of the road

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.653
seeking two moon, hit by a car.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.490
My wife Elfie and myself, we
just thought let's do something

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.323
and we did it.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:19.530
I put this on the trees and
on the sign on the roads

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.270
that people know in the night

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.643
where can we deliver the Puffins

00:06:23.643 --> 00:06:25.540
and where are the headquarters.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.370
And then I put this one here,

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.320
they are illuminator for the cars.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.650
You can put them on the car.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.610
You need always a short
good name of doing something

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.690
and Puffin Patrol says everything.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:38.560
Puffin Patrol, ding
dong, unnecessary light.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.325
It's Puffin saving time, come in.

00:06:41.325 --> 00:06:42.900
- Okay.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.890
- So we started to buy gloves...

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:45.760
Here's my gloves.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:46.910
Butterfly nets..

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.740
In the car I do have the net.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:49.600
And the flashlight...

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.285
I do have the flashlight.

00:06:51.285 --> 00:06:52.465
Elfie, are you ready?

00:06:52.465 --> 00:06:54.187
- Yep.
- Good.

00:06:54.187 --> 00:06:56.820
And Elfie and me went out the first time

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.363
to save the little birds.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.570
So we go from the flashlight
from the left side

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:04.880
with a net from the right side.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.170
The bird look at the flashlight,
I go from the left side,

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.480
and then we got it.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.530
We put them then in a little cradle,

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.730
let's them here and
next day we let them go.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.390
We drove from nine o'clock

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.360
to almost one o'clock in the night.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.880
My smart wife told me,
Juergen, there's not enough.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.050
We should not do this alone.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.260
We should bring in some people.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.443
And then it started.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.890
It's 10 o'clock.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:35.260
It depends every day how many we saving.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.960
It could be 10, it could be 20.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.240
Every night out, we put
them then in a little cradle

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.923
and then the next
morning, they're released.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.274
Driving around, you're walking around,

00:07:47.274 --> 00:07:52.213
low years 100, sometimes
800, 900 every night.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.510
Driving one o'clock to two o'clock

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.530
and people were knocking on my door

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.640
and bringing birds in front of the door.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.572
It's Puffin saving time.

00:08:01.572 --> 00:08:05.020
Driving around, walking around.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:08.530
I'm saying we saved over
a total more than 10,000.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.890
Sometimes the whole
shed was full of birds.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.560
It's Puffin saving time.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:14.800
Every night.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.633
Wait, wait, wait.

00:08:15.633 --> 00:08:18.344
Nine to 11, and 11 to 12.

00:08:18.344 --> 00:08:19.930
It's Puffin saving time.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:20.813
Every night.

00:08:21.893 --> 00:08:22.728
- [Woman] Puffin Patrol.

00:08:22.728 --> 00:08:23.561
- Yes.

00:08:23.561 --> 00:08:25.170
Then it came to our mind...

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.100
Wait, wait, wait.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.403
It's too much, too big
for me and for us alone.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.970
We were so happy that
we have now this spread

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.320
to Canadian Park and Wilderness Society,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.212
and they decided to take
over the Puffin Patrol

00:08:39.212 --> 00:08:42.740
as their issue.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.190
- I don't think we can
ever fill Juergen's shoes.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.530
So thank you for coming out.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:50.320
When you have a program like this,

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.572
you start to find out in your community

00:08:51.572 --> 00:08:53.820
who is conservation-minded,

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:56.823
who maybe they feel that
this is isn't an issue.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.910
My name is Suzanne Dooley.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.400
I'm with the Canadian Parks
and Wilderness Society.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.870
We help coordinate and
facilitate this program.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:08.030
To this day even now it seems
to be a very good news story.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.510
Still there is a bit
of opposition as well.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.660
We can't please everybody
but I know there is

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.960
a lot of opposition within the community

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.980
for and against like every project.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.560
Some of our core volunteers that we had,

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.683
they see that and they
feel that as well too.

00:09:28.323 --> 00:09:30.906
(radio static)

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:35.340
- [Presenter] Sometimes the
province makes the national news

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.698
for all the wrong reasons.

00:09:36.698 --> 00:09:39.980
That was the case last week
in what is an ironic twist.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:42.420
Witless Bay did indeed
make the national news

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:43.800
because of what looked like an effort

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:46.240
to silence the citizens on social media.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.670
Witless Bay town council
had unanimously passed

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:51.690
a motion to look into retaining
independent criminal lawyer

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.950
to review a recent
social media accusations

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:55.470
against the current town council.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.960
That didn't sit very well with Lorna Yard

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.840
who has been embroiled in a battle

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.900
with council over the
development of Ragged Beach.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.300
Lorna joins me live in the studios.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.203
Nice to see you, Lorna.

00:10:03.203 --> 00:10:04.570
(laughing)

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:07.173
- My reputation in town, well.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.723
I probably wouldn't want to imagine that.

00:10:13.343 --> 00:10:14.240
But I don't know.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.970
I just have to think about
that one for a second.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.653
I am surprised by that question.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:24.800
- I think Lorna wouldn't
describe herself as an activist.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.190
- Lorna is very much involved
in the local community

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.010
because she's a fighter.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.240
And she fights for the environmental.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.258
- And I know that she is
one of the strong opponents

00:10:35.258 --> 00:10:38.540
of the Ragged Beach group and
actually has a Facebook page.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.861
- She runs the Ragged Beach Newsline,

00:10:40.861 --> 00:10:44.690
which is all the news
about what's going on

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:45.593
and so forth.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.810
- [Lorna] I have this
streak in me where I just,

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.630
I do stand up for things I believe in.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.920
And so I never really get involved

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.020
in the Puffin Patrol too much

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.123
until the Ragged Beach threat happened.

00:10:58.271 --> 00:11:01.271
(loud horn blowing)

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:18.470
So Ragged Beach is a dark coast right now.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.851
There are no houses, there
is no light pollution.

00:11:20.851 --> 00:11:25.243
And it is directly across
from the Ecological Reserve.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.350
And it would never occur to
us to build a house there.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:33.550
Because if you put in a
development on the coastline

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.210
I believe and many of us believe

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.473
it will be absolutely
catastrophic for the reserve.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.880
But when you get people
coming in from outside

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.330
they just view a piece of land and say,

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.460
wow, this is amazing, I
would like to live here.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.750
And so we have a group of
people fighting so hard

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:54.940
for what we see as the benefits

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.910
of protecting our environment
and protecting the Puffins,

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.730
and then we have people who
are really just concerned

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:02.883
with profit and monetizing coastlines.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:06.540
- Oh, there's some berries.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.610
Not quite ripe but

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.987
some are more than others.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:21.780
So my name is AnnMarie Churchill.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.460
I'm a landowner here in
the Ragged Beach area

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:25.890
and a Newfoundlander.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.796
Yeah, so I grew up in Newfoundland.

00:12:27.796 --> 00:12:31.540
and I grew up about 30 minutes from here

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.983
in the city of St. Johns.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.810
And so when we came back
we just really wanted to be

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:41.213
close to the ocean and nature.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.170
So that's how we ended up here.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.840
We actually were hiking here one day

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.120
and looked it up when we got home

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.520
and there was land for sale.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.310
We were told from the very beginning

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.510
there'll be a group there
who are going to oppose you.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.630
They've opposed in the
past to anyone who's tried

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.260
to develop in this area
because they don't want

00:12:58.260 --> 00:12:59.510
any houses down here.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:00.540
But it's private property.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.290
So we thought, okay,
well, we'll deal with it.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:04.560
What do we need to do to make this okay?

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:05.393
Like what do you want?

00:13:05.393 --> 00:13:07.580
And they said, we're
not here to negotiate,

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.413
we're here to stop you.

00:13:08.413 --> 00:13:09.812
We want no development down here.

00:13:09.812 --> 00:13:13.790
- When the Churchill's
put in their application

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:17.000
in 2010 to have that re-zoned,

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.080
at the time there was just a
collective scream of outrage

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.070
from the province, from the world.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.610
And so this right here is Ragged Beach.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.220
So you can see that
this is directly across.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:29.890
Now here you'll see, this is Witless Bay,

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.600
and here you'll see this
subdivision back here.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.590
So if you look at this subdivision

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.110
and you look at Ragged Beach,

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.650
you can see how close Ragged Beach is.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.650
And you just look straight
out, you're looking straight

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:43.130
at the Witless Bay Ecological Reserve.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.900
The island is directly across from it.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.627
We live in a town of 1,200 people,

00:13:46.627 --> 00:13:49.660
and our town council
got over 1,400 letters

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.020
against re-zoning that area.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.650
They got 11 in support.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:56.040
I have here a letter from Billmont Vicky.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.090
Bill, he is a seabird biologist.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.880
He's known the world over

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.690
that of all the ecological
seabird reserves

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.377
in Newfoundland and Labrador,

00:14:05.377 --> 00:14:07.884
the Witless Bay Ecological Reserve

00:14:07.884 --> 00:14:11.857
is the one in closest proximity
to coastal communities

00:14:11.857 --> 00:14:14.240
and is the one most at risk

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.060
to human activities and development.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:18.270
This is a letter from a descendant

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:19.530
of a Witless Bay resident.

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.270
This is a man who lives in New York.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.107
A subdivision with more to come

00:14:23.107 --> 00:14:25.840
and the most achingly
beautiful stretch of coastline

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.410
in Newfoundland.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:28.420
Beautiful...

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.980
Not just because our eyes tell us so

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.100
but because our hearts do as well.

00:14:44.257 --> 00:14:45.850
And those letters were just ignored.

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:47.415
Our provincial government ignored 'em.

00:14:47.415 --> 00:14:50.403
And that's when the war
in this town started.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.901
- [Woman] Good evening, everyone.

00:14:54.901 --> 00:14:57.769
We have a long agenda
tonight, so you'll have to

00:14:57.769 --> 00:14:59.860
just bear with me.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:00.930
Okay, good evening.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.480
- [Man] I'd like to take
the time to appoint board

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.510
to concern legal matters of town.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:08.323
And I'd like to pass the motion.

00:15:09.475 --> 00:15:11.474
These are concerns and
motions that I want to put...

00:15:11.474 --> 00:15:12.555
(banging)

00:15:12.555 --> 00:15:13.939
I require a second, do I have a seconder?

00:15:13.939 --> 00:15:15.940
Do I have a seconder?
- Council Gary.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:16.807
Excuse me.

00:15:16.807 --> 00:15:17.945
- [Man] Do I have a seconder?

00:15:17.945 --> 00:15:19.002
- [Woman] Sit down, please.

00:15:19.002 --> 00:15:20.437
- Do I have a seconder?
- You're out of order.

00:15:20.437 --> 00:15:22.442
- [Man] Council, with recommendations...

00:15:22.442 --> 00:15:25.359
(mumbled shouting)

00:15:33.993 --> 00:15:37.493
(soft instrumental music)

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:48.863
- [Lorna] Local town council
here does not subscribe to

00:15:48.863 --> 00:15:52.330
issues of environmentalism

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.810
or sustaining your natural assets.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:58.400
Our local council, their
mandate is development,

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:02.710
big development, big business,
that's their mandate.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:05.220
Where there's more development
there's more lights.

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:08.823
And so we want to protect Ragged Beach.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:12.297
- There are subdivisions in Witless Bay

00:16:12.297 --> 00:16:14.750
as there are in all communities,

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.949
and I think when you start
new projects or whatever

00:16:16.949 --> 00:16:19.800
you look back and say I
wish I had done something

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:21.400
a little bit different.

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.990
Clear cutting maybe in a
couple of the divisions here

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:26.323
or subdivisions may have been excessive.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.020
But there is something to be said

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.620
for the private land owners that live

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:35.540
within that line of fire.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:37.710
Who am I to say that they can't build?

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.610
And I'm an individual resident;

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.260
I'm not speaking for the council.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.663
So yeah, I mean, I wouldn't
speak against them.

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:50.460
- I think it's insane that it seems to me

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.550
any reasonable person that
would walk down on that beach

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.670
and say let's put up some houses has got

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.470
something wrong with their thinking.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:02.710
- I was shocked the first
time they called us developer.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:05.450
And I think this group
know that that's a word

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.950
that gets people so they've used it,

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.900
they've called us "the developers."

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.870
No, we're land owners,
that's what I call me.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:13.113
I'm a land owner, and I
want a house on my land.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.470
I would say absolutely it's not a story

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.610
of development versus environment.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:23.660
I think it is a story of
legitimate environmental causes

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.950
being hijacked to stop
some private land owners

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:30.030
in a small area Newfoundland
from using their land.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:32.648
Their argument is if we put a house here

00:17:32.648 --> 00:17:35.010
then we're adding lighting

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.240
and we're adding development to the area.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.240
And my argument is that Newfoundlanders

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.950
have always built along the shoreline,

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.550
but it can be done respectfully.

00:17:46.158 --> 00:17:47.900
In this town, people have
built lots of development.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:51.130
But what we've done here
is 1,000 times different.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.620
We didn't clear cut.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.657
At the most we get a gazebo
or a house for our boys,

00:17:55.657 --> 00:17:57.760
that's it.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:02.070
I don't want subdivisions;
I don't want hotels. I want

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:03.550
peace. I feel I'm an environmentalist,

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:05.100
so I've had to question myself,

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:07.280
is this going to hurt the birds?

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.893
I don't believe one house is.

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:12.470
- This is where I do all my thinking.

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:14.113
This is where I come when I'm

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:19.003
feeling a bit stressed.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.310
- [AnnMarie] The Puffins
have been hijacked.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.310
Like I used to love the Puffin cause,

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.330
now I hear it and I almost get nauseated

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.910
because I know it's been hijacked

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.080
by people who know how to do it,

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.670
who are good marketers,
who are good sellers,

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.160
who do use social media.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.300
So we have been vilified.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.640
This has been put on Facebook,

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:38.786
that we're horrible people
and they spin something

00:18:38.786 --> 00:18:40.673
to get their own way.

00:18:43.476 --> 00:18:45.643
(buzzing)

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:16.080
- [Man] There's always in
small towns personal conflicts,

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:19.200
and usually they settle
it over a period of time.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.606
But right now because of
social media and Facebook,

00:19:21.606 --> 00:19:24.780
there seems to be quite a lot of texting

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.993
and tweeting going on.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:28.600
- [AnnMarie] The scary part is that

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.240
that amplification is dangerous.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.350
Like someone said, oh,
they don't own that land.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.040
We'll burn down their gazebo,
and I worry about that

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.900
because if you get people who
don't think things through

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:40.380
or may not be stable, that could happen.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.140
Like I think there could
be real consequences,

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.910
and I've said if this continues to go on,

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:45.360
somebody's going to get hurt.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:54.700
- You know, I haven't
always acted honorably

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:57.540
and their have been times when frustration

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:58.973
and stress got to me.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.680
Puffins can't speak for themselves.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.320
Rocks and beaches can't
speak for themselves.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:09.610
And whether not my head's
screwed on straight,

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.153
it's up for debate, but
my intentions are true.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.270
So we're going back,

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.660
we're driving down
Gallus Cove Road here now

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:22.493
in Witless Bay.

00:20:22.493 --> 00:20:24.390
We're going to go down to Ragged Beach.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:27.063
It's at the very end of this road.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.520
I always draw my strength and my comfort

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.490
from Ragged Beach.

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.780
So that's why I feel so strongly.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:37.730
So we're coming here a lot in the fall

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.220
and generally in the off season.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:42.360
But during the summer, not so much anymore

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:45.683
just because of the whole
situation surrounding us.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.434
- [AnnMarie] I can't stay
reasonable and rational,

00:20:56.434 --> 00:20:58.980
and I don't want to lose control.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.730
I don't want to be upset
and angry all the time.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.310
I want to be reasonable,
and I want to understand

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.410
where they're coming from.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.580
So my fantasy is we'll work together,

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.313
but I don't think that will happen.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:20.130
- So as you can see,
we're right at the feet

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.220
of the ecological reserve.

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.310
We're directly across from it.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:26.720
So, our position is that if
you put development in here

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.570
I mean it's going to be
shining right at the reserve.

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:32.363
And we're already facing
a lot of challenges.

00:21:33.623 --> 00:21:34.657
- [Man] You can all come out there.

00:21:34.657 --> 00:21:35.490
- Izzy.

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.720
- You must be Lorna.
- Uh oh.

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:37.710
- Hi, I'm AnnMarie.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:39.660
- Hi, how are you?

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:41.480
- I'm the person that you
love to hate all the time.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:42.740
- I don't hate you.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:43.573
- Well some of the personal stuff man...

00:21:43.573 --> 00:21:45.900
- We agree to dis..
- Holy cow.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.627
Is pretty wild when you don't know us

00:21:47.627 --> 00:21:49.230
and have never met us.

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:51.720
- We didn't start the fire.
- A bit surprising.

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:54.500
Oh well, we got mad and it went personal

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:56.040
so I'm just saying you don't know us.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.770
So it'd be great to get to
know each other sometime

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:58.824
so you actually...

00:21:58.824 --> 00:21:59.657
- Well, you know, when you bought the land

00:21:59.657 --> 00:22:00.490
you knew you couldn't build here.

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:01.490
- That's not true.

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:03.650
- I have a quote in a
newspaper that you said that.

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:06.220
- I have, we have approval
and principle from the land.

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:08.020
We had a lawyer investigate.

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:09.440
And you've written that you even saw

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.690
we had the approval and principle.

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:13.250
So that's beside the point at this point.

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:14.617
I have asked environmentalists,

00:22:14.617 --> 00:22:18.560
one house up here as far
away as we've offered to be

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:20.130
give another 100 feet from the trail,

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:22.030
will that have any impact on the birds

00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:23.480
and the answer was,

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:25.970
three houses in an environmental enclave

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:27.860
will not hurt the birds whatsoever.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:28.693
- That's great.

00:22:28.693 --> 00:22:30.430
- You can't tell me
that one house back here

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:32.900
with hooded lights,

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:35.510
environmentally sensitive,
is hurting the Puffins.

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:38.080
I think what you're doing is
your hijacking the Puffins

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:39.980
and the East coast Trail to keep this land

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:41.220
for your private crap.
- So you're related..

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:42.500
So your teaming up with Michelle.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:43.860
That's why she flipped out 'cause she's...

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:45.380
- Who's Michelle?

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:46.410
This is what you do.

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:47.670
You do all this personal stuff.

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:49.010
I don't even know who Michelle is.

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:49.843
I have no idea

00:22:49.843 --> 00:22:50.676
who you're talking about.
- Anyway.

00:22:50.676 --> 00:22:51.850
- But you just said that

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:53.480
and tomorrow you'll have on Facebook

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.620
that we're somehow in with
someone doing something weird.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:57.950
You guys have given nothing...
- You have gone to meetings,

00:22:57.950 --> 00:22:59.490
You have screamed at people,
- We have tried everything.

00:22:59.490 --> 00:23:00.780
- You harassed at me.
- Because...

00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:02.230
- I sat in a courtroom with you..

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:03.900
- Lorna, please don't, please
don't do that in my face.

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.810
- I sat in a courtroom when you made fun

00:23:04.810 --> 00:23:06.290
of a disabled senior citizen.

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:08.270
- Actually I'm not even going
answer that, that's not true.

00:23:08.270 --> 00:23:09.103
- I heard you behind me laughing at him.

00:23:09.103 --> 00:23:09.936
- That is absolutely not true.

00:23:09.936 --> 00:23:11.180
- I heard you.
- We didn't even know

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:12.420
who was on the stand.
- I heard you

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:13.450
back there laughing.
- Lorna you have no idea

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:14.850
what we're talking about.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:16.050
That's what I mean, what you do,

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:18.030
instead of the facts, you go personal

00:23:18.030 --> 00:23:19.140
and you try to destroy people,

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:20.110
but we're not willing to
give up our land over it yet.

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:21.930
- It's not me, it's the town.

00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:23.180
Nobody wants this...
- You just did it

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.140
about 10 times here,
- Nobody wants

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:24.973
this area developed.
- where I try to talk

00:23:24.973 --> 00:23:26.870
and you start attacking me.
- It's not me.

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.720
- But you're the one doing this attacking.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:29.657
This isn't rational, it's not a good...

00:23:29.657 --> 00:23:31.040
- How am I attacking you now

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:32.490
when I'm telling you you can use your land

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:34.840
as you've always used
it, as it was designated.

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:36.880
You have no access, and
that's just the facts.

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:39.293
- I'm sorry it doesn't get
any better than that Lorna.

00:23:57.483 --> 00:23:58.566
- Come on Iz.

00:23:59.820 --> 00:24:03.820
(banging and soft violin music)

00:24:15.277 --> 00:24:17.890
- [Juergen] I think this is
a very, very important place

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:19.800
for nature and for the animals.

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.216
But as always, when you're in the middle

00:24:22.216 --> 00:24:26.433
of the eye of a cyclone, you're
not seeing the whole thing.

00:24:29.770 --> 00:24:31.923
- [Woman] So it's something
worth fighting for?

00:24:33.260 --> 00:24:36.350
- Something worth dying for, almost.

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:37.806
They think that they're going to wear

00:24:37.806 --> 00:24:40.910
the people who want to preserve that down.

00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:42.540
It's not going to happen.

00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:45.100
It's a battle for me
that's not going to end.

00:24:45.100 --> 00:24:46.970
And I don't think it's going to end

00:24:46.970 --> 00:24:48.270
for a lot of other people.

00:24:50.626 --> 00:24:52.460
- I think when you have controversy,

00:24:52.460 --> 00:24:55.590
there'll always be a side of
it that's sensationalized.

00:24:55.590 --> 00:24:57.960
I would hope that we
can find a common ground

00:24:57.960 --> 00:25:00.400
for all groups that have concerns,

00:25:00.400 --> 00:25:03.500
that someday soon we can
get those concerns out

00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:06.390
and discuss them and
come to terms with them.

00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:11.800
- [Lorna] I have missed a lot
personally and there's times

00:25:11.800 --> 00:25:13.760
it's been really, really tough

00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:15.850
to the point where you
know, I had episodes

00:25:15.850 --> 00:25:17.920
of really severe depression

00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:20.160
and there were times when
I just said to myself

00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:21.632
and everybody else, I'm done, I'm done,

00:25:21.632 --> 00:25:23.460
and you just come back.

00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:27.060
But you know, there's also been
really amazing things, too.

00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:29.090
Friendships have been made.

00:25:29.090 --> 00:25:31.350
But at the end of the
day it's not about me.

00:25:31.350 --> 00:25:33.710
It's about Ragged Beach;
it's about Puffins;

00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:37.530
it's about wildlife; it's
about this spectacular reserve;

00:25:37.530 --> 00:25:38.680
that's what it's about.

00:25:40.220 --> 00:25:42.180
- [AnnMarie] I don't know, I
mean maybe I'll change my mind.

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:43.610
Maybe they will push us out of here

00:25:43.610 --> 00:25:45.630
but I would feel bad about that.

00:25:45.630 --> 00:25:47.860
I feel like we need to hold our ground

00:25:47.860 --> 00:25:51.020
but try to keep it civilized.

00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:52.320
I talk to people more,

00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:54.360
but I'm trying to be helpful about it,

00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:57.040
let people know the truth
and ignore social media.

00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:58.340
I don't know where to go with that.

00:25:58.340 --> 00:26:01.410
So I kind of have some
hope if we could hold out.

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:04.521
- [Juergen] The ecological
system is so sensitive here;

00:26:04.521 --> 00:26:05.520
it is all here.

00:26:05.520 --> 00:26:08.650
It's really here; you can
feel it, you can see it.

00:26:08.650 --> 00:26:11.670
But we're there, Puffin Patrol,
and all the organization,

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:13.110
we try to protect them.

00:26:13.110 --> 00:26:14.810
And it's growing, it's doing well.

00:26:16.390 --> 00:26:17.820
- [Woman] What's your dream situation

00:26:17.820 --> 00:26:19.260
for how this all ends up?

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:20.660
- Let me quote Jack Nicholson.

00:26:20.660 --> 00:26:23.080
He told me Juergen, in a perfect world,

00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:25.440
everything would be really perfect.

00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:27.010
But we're not in a perfect world.

00:26:27.010 --> 00:26:29.480
So what can I do, what can I change?

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:32.630
Of course, I do want to
stop the Puffin Patrol.

00:26:32.630 --> 00:26:35.330
Of course I would not see
any dead birds anymore.

00:26:35.330 --> 00:26:37.900
Of course, I would like
to have people respect

00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:38.822
and think like this.

00:26:38.822 --> 00:26:41.000
But the world isn't though.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:43.023
It is as it is, so.

00:26:48.052 --> 00:26:50.219
(buzzing)

00:26:58.282 --> 00:27:00.365
(mooing)

